      {
        "id": 87777,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-05T18:28:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Alright, 3-2 in favor of checking up on what you accomplished. &nbsp;You all seemed to follow your characters.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span><span>“You’re all about timeline security now, but for goodness sake you took a civil War veteran gave him crazy weapons and sent him back to shoot monsters, how are we going to do anything worse than that?”</span></span></p><p><span><span>Anthony could hear the arguing, and he had a feeling Pauline would get her way. &nbsp;There was just something about her, it wasn’t easy to tell her no. &nbsp;She just had to convince the Robots, they were the time travellers. &nbsp;Legacy had lost signal with her time device in the future, she said that meant they had succeeded, or at least created a future where it was never invented.</span></span></p><p><span><span>Anthony wanted to go, his friends were gone, the people he knew didn’t exist. &nbsp;Well they did, but not as he knew them. &nbsp;Hopefully they were happy. &nbsp;Hopefully he was happy. &nbsp;It was weird being “Temporal Tumbleweeds” as Jim had called him and Graves. &nbsp;They were the remnants of their timelines, only around because they weren’t in their timelines to be destroyed, or something. Now they got to drift, knowing anything they did that affected other people could disrupt the timelines all over again.</span></span></p><p><span><span>If he did have to disappear, at least he wouldn't be alone. . .</span></span></p><p><span><span>“Hey, Daydreamer, wake up.” &nbsp;Anthony snapped his head up to see Pauline smiling at him.</span></span></p><p><span><span>“We’re going.”</span></span></p><p><span><span>. . .</span></span></p><p><span><span>Insula Primalis. &nbsp;He’d never heard of it. &nbsp;Apparently they could re-emerge there and not have any risk of upsetting the timeline, except for maybe some prehistoric creatures, as much out of place as they were.</span></span></p><p><span><span>They could transport there, and scan the TV and Radio waves to find out if they had succeeded. &nbsp;It wasn’t quite what he had hoped for, but he had a feeling Pauline wasn’t done yet.</span></span></p><p><span><span>“Temporal axis aligned with spatial co-ordinates, begin Temporal Transition.”</span></span></p><p><span><span>The air fizzled, and everything went white. . .</span></span></p><p><span><span>. . . </span></span></p><p><span><span>There was something touching his face. . . no, slapping it, and hard.</span></span></p><p><span><span>“Alright I’m up, stop it!” &nbsp;Anthony’s face was stinging with pain, “Damn Graves, you practically broke my jaw.”</span></span></p><p><span><span>He looked around, they were in a jungle alright.</span></span></p><p><span><span>“You sure this is the North Pole?” he asked groggily, already sweating in the damp heat.</span></span></p><p><span><span>“Shhh. . . we are trying to listen.”</span></span></p><p><span><span>Legacy was huddled over the transceiver as Con scanned communication channels.</span></span></p><p><span><span>“Everything appears to be alright. . . Except, Oh No!”</span></span></p><p><span><span>“What is it?” Legacy asked.</span></span></p><p><span><span>Con didn’t need to answer.</span></span></p><p><span><span>There was an audible 'POP' behind them, and the sound of something big moving through the tree branches.</span></span></p><p><span><span>“Hello,” came the loud and thickly accented Spanish voice, “My name is </span><span>Maria Helena Teresa Fafila Servanda Jimena Mansuara Paterna Domenga Gelvira Placia Sendina Belita Eufemia Columba Gontina Aldonza Mafalda Cristina Tegrida de Falcon, hand over the Robots and you will be left alive.”</span></span></p><p><span><span>“Oh man,” Anthony muttered, “here we go again.”</span></span></p><div>Stay tuned for Episode #9 \"The Pirates of Dinosaur Island.\"</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>The whole arc is going to be 12 Episodes, so 4 fights left. &nbsp;Anyone want to guess the 3 fights remaining after this next one?</div>",
